--------------------------- Changelog -----------------------------

1.0.d - UNRELEASED

General
Added - Version Checker support (changelog and download in LunaLib and triOS)
Adjusted - Off-screen ripples and Fisherman lamps are no longer drawn
Adjusted - Lower frame cost for epic and legendary trails out of lamplight
Fixed - Ripple and rupture shaders no longer cause stutter and VRAM growth
Fixed - Closed ruptures no longer keep their ripples in memory and the save
Fixed - The aquarium no longer slows every frame looking for the colony screen

Fisherman
Added - Treasure rumour: after the tutorial, find the Fisherman's lost chest
Added - Treasure rumour: the chest comes up on lamp catches there (30% each, certain on the 4th, then every 2nd)
Added - Treasure rumour: the compass inside earns the Glitter Lens schematic
Added - Treasure rumour: more bycatch until the compass is back, then for two months after buying the lens
Added - Lose the compass and the Fisherman tracks it down or pays you anyway
Added - Captain's epic: a captain whose Breach Lights failed needs yours
Added - Captain's epic: keep your lights on within 6,000 units of the star for 15s, then harpoon it
Added - Captain's epic: pays a Stigmata, plus a harpoon schematic and 3 range data if landed
Added - Report back to the Fisherman for the Needle Sensor schematic
Added - Wounded epic: hunt one circling a planet in a nearby empty system
Added - Wounded epic: it swims at half speed once woken
Added - Wounded epic: losing it or your lights restarts the hunt
Added - Wounded epic: pays epic range data and a lead on a Reliquary for sale
Added - A bar drunk trades his Reliquary for 3 epic fish, 2 with a story point
Added - Listen for rumours: report your first legendary for a Monstrance
Added - The next three legendary reports pay the three fishing ship blueprints
Added - An early legendary report ends the earlier jobs and pays their rewards
Added - "Hunting the legendary fish" intel lists the legendaries you know
Adjusted - Tidied Fisherman tutorial lines and the old captain's farewell
Fixed - Asking about the ROD now explains it instead of repeating a scene

Fishing ships
Added - Stigmata-class Harpoon Tug: fast, heavy destroyer, 180° omni shield, fighter bay
Added - Reliquary-class LYNE Tender: slow carrier cruiser, LYNE salvage drones
Added - Monstrance-class Breach Trawler: cruiser with two built-in Breach Lights
Added - Standard machine gun loadouts, used by custom production and autofit
Added - Fishing ships add a second Harpoon, Drone Core or Lens Array slot
Added - They come with the Retrieval Head, Lifting Rig and Fanned Array
Note - The Lifting Rig and the Salvage Trawl cannot share the rig
Added - Tug Drive Field: +1 maximum burn per active Stigmata in your fleet
Added - Tug Drive Field: +20% acceleration for the first Stigmata, half that for each next one
Note - No effect during Sustained Burn
Added - Tug Harpoon: 2 charges (12s each), 400 kinetic damage, 900 range, no friendly damage
Added - Tug Harpoon: a hull hit tethers any ship or wreck for 20s, dragging the lighter one more
Added - Tug Harpoon: glances off shields, at most twice
Added - Tug Harpoon: firing again lets go without spending a charge
Added - Haul Drive (Stigmata system): up to 2.5x mass for 5s, +150% acceleration, +50% turn rate and speed
Added - Haul Drive: 3 charges, one back every 20s
Added - AI Stigmatas harpoon exposed or fleeing enemies into friendly guns
Added - AI Stigmatas never fire into facing shields or past friends
Added - AI Stigmatas use the Haul Drive on heavy catches and to escape
Added - AI Stigmatas drag swarmed or overloaded friends back to safety
Added - With a Reliquary in battle, enemy fighters leave wrecks 75% of the time for 30s
Added - LYNE drones tow fighter wrecks within 8,000 units to the Reliquary's store (max 10)
Added - Stored fighters restore in combat and stay aboard between battles
Note - The store empties if the Reliquary leaves your fleet
Note - Fighters recovered in a simulator battle never reach the store
Added - Salvage Launch (Reliquary system): launches every restored fighter
Added - Launched fighters return to rearm and are lost if destroyed
Added - AI Reliquaries launch with two fighters ready and an enemy in reach
Added - Flying a Reliquary lists its recovered fighters above the ship display
Added - Refit shows recovered fighters as up to 4 locked bays
Added - Reliquary refit option "Recovered fighters" lists and discards them
Note - Discarded fighters are gone for good and give no LPC
Added - Setting for Reliquary recovered fighter capacity (10 by default)
Added - Setting for Reliquary fighter wreck chance (75% by default)
Added - Breach Lights (Monstrance system): toggle, 1.5s charge-up, 4s cooldown, 5% hard flux/s
Added - Breach Lights: two lights sweep out to 900 units and hold on enemy ships
Added - Breach Lights: each light raises a mote about once a second (max 8, 6s each)
Added - Breach Lights: enemy ships touching a mote lose shield or phase for 1s
Added - Breach Lights: motes destroy enemy fighters and missiles
Added - AI Monstrances use the lights below 60% flux with an enemy in reach, stop above 85%

Epic and legendary fish
Adjusted - Epic fish come up only under Breach Lights, no longer in ROD ruptures
Adjusted - Epic fish drift slowly until a harpoon hit in a lit beam wakes them
Adjusted - Awake epics raise a one-charge shield and swim more erratically
Adjusted - Epics stay in reach only while lit and drift off past 3,000 units
Adjusted - An awake epic is gone once you leave the system
Adjusted - Only the harpoon lands epics, ROD drones leave them alone
Adjusted - Legendary rumour intel shows the told name until you catch the fish
Fixed - Epic and legendary shields now fade out with the fish when it dives

Breach Lights
Added - Setting for surfaced lamp-fish speed (100% by default)
Added - Settings to turn off fish surfacing or keep the old straight course
Adjusted - Ordinary fish surface in Breach Lights and swim in their own style
Adjusted - The Tracking Gimbal and its upgrade follow surfaced fish

Equipment
Added - Glitter Lens: Lens Array module, doubles bycatch under Breach Lights
Note - Its schematic comes only from the Fisherman's treasure rumour
Added - The Neutrino Lens shows quest fish as gold spikes, whatever their rarity
Adjusted - Equipment modules cost one tier more (now 25,000 to 45,000 credits)
Adjusted - Equipment modules can no longer be paid for with common fish alone
Adjusted - The Retrieval Head, Fanned Array and Lifting Rig are no longer sold
Note - They come with the fishing ships now, copies you own are kept
Adjusted - Neutrino Lens spikes also need the Breach Lights on
Removed - Breach Coupler (withdrawn for now, a fitted one does nothing)

Harpoon and ROD
Added - The Harpoon breaks Industrial Evolution meteors and returns to the fleet
Note - Needs Industrial Evolution 4.2.a or newer
Adjusted - Harpoon and ROD aiming is blocked while an IE missile is aimed
Note - Needs Industrial Evolution 4.2.a or newer
Fixed - Aiming the Harpoon or ROD from its button no longer leaves save data
Fixed - Held Harpoon and ROD hotkeys fire on release, even if the bar changed
Removed - Harpoon and ROD aiming debug lines in starsector.log

Fishing jobs
Adjusted - Accepted job markers are steady gold (offers still pulse)
Adjusted - Fight Night: fee option reads "Take the rewards." and lists them
Fixed - Fleets with a quest or marked important no longer take fishing jobs too
Fixed - Attacking a mercenary camp now costs reputation with the independents

Distress calls
Adjusted - Distress calls wait while another mod's distress call is live
Fixed - Distress calls over 1.6 LY away now show in intel instead of vanishing

Codex
Adjusted - Codex entries from range data alone show no fish icon until caught
Fixed - Codex list icons no longer stay blank until shown elsewhere

Aquarium
Adjusted - Manage the aquarium is one panel: tank, counts, display switch, backdrops
Adjusted - Backdrops are picked from picture tiles, the paged menu is gone

Outfitter
Adjusted - Equipment tabs follow the same rig order as the Upgrades tabs
Adjusted - Shopping list dot centred between the row's edge and its name
Fixed - The Outfitter no longer opens on a locked shelf with an empty list
Fixed - Undoing a purchase from another tab now shows that item's shelf
Fixed - Buying a module for both rigs now clears its mark on the other shelf
Fixed - The route planner no longer lists the same module twice
Fixed - Equipment with no fish price no longer shows a dead FIT button
Fixed - Equipment help no longer mentions an undrawn single-use marker

Text and UI
Adjusted - Clearer fishing settings and AddFish help
Adjusted - Fisherman sale screen: "Pack into crates" moved to the Sell row
Note - Catch.Release now requires PatchLib
Fixed - Chart requests now describe the marked specimen's mote as gold, not cyan

Development
Adjusted - AddFish takes an ID or name, then quantity, quality and coherence

1.0.c

Quests and payments
Fixed - A camp fleet that loses a fight to you gives up the rupture and leaves, instead of holding it until destroyed
Fixed - Job intel names the market and star system to deliver to, and switches to "Return to" once you have the catch; a cleared camp job points back to the fisher once the proof is aboard
Fixed - Automatic job and Outfitter payments no longer consume legendary fish.
Removed - Disabled legendary tribute at Kanta's Den pending dialogue replacement.

Fleet interactions
Changed - Contract hunters respond less often to single harpoon hits, but may pursue unpaid repair bills or fleeing after identification following a dark hit. Paying the fine calls them off.
Changed - Crews with unpaid repair bills now report you to local patrols instead of chasing you. All patrols in the system demand payment on sight until the fine is paid.

Crablobab
Added - Crablobab sells Party Horn after acquiring Celebration Charges, followed by Crab Fanfare. Both replace the catch sound and can be previewed before purchase and selected in the Outfitter.

Equipment
Added - Neutrino Lens module for the Lens Array. Shows rare, epic and legendary patterns as rarity-coloured Neutrino Detector spikes. Grants the detector if missing.
Fixed - Needle Sensor ripples are larger, brighter and visible at greater zoom distances.

Treasure
Added - Uncommon fishing chests have a 25% chance to contain unknown range data alongside normal loot, including with the Lifting Rig.
Changed - Recovered treasure now has aligned quantities; range data displays as "Range data: <fish>".

Harpoon
Adjusted - Harpoons hitting shields no longer play the catch sound.

Legendaries
Removed - Failed Quorum catches no longer spawn 12 extra decoys.
Fixed - Dormant epics and legendaries now leave trails under breach lights.
Fixed - Loading saves with Lantern Jack surfaced in the current system no longer crashes.
Fixed - Reduced performance cost of epic and legendary trails under breach lights.
Fixed - Legendary floating text use shield or mote colour instead of a generic UI highlight
Added - Lantern Jack now coils for 0.3 seconds within 300 units of a mote, then dashes through it to feed (also: added vfx)

Aquarium
Fixed - Corrected aquarium swimming orientation for 13 species, including Dopefish and several legendaries.

1.0.b

General
Added - Temporary industry image

Fisherman
Fixed - Nearby settlements no longer prevent the Fisherman from approaching you for the tutorial
Fixed - Finishing the Fisherman's "Why a fish?" questions no longer shows an empty Continue before "You could have told me this before I started."
Fixed - Fisherman tutorial lessons no longer send you to systems with a neutron star
Adjusted - The Fisherman's first lesson now points at the rupture closest to him
Added - Selling fish to the Fisherman can unpack crates again after using "Pack into crates"
Fixed - Hovering the "Pack into crates" button in the Fisherman sale screen no longer repeats the click sound
Fixed - Undo in the Fisherman's range data shop takes back every purchase in sequence, newest first, like the Outfitter
Adjusted - Buncha dialogue
Fixed - "Set autopilot" on tutorial and chart request intel now targets a visiting Fisherman in your current system instead of a boat elsewhere

Fish
Added - New portraits for 16 fish that had placeholders until now
Added - Dopefish, a rare Epic catch that barely moves and is very easy to land
Fixed - System fish counts no longer include a species that never spawns there, which made a full system show 16 species
Fixed - A star system never offers more than 15 species; a legendary in a full system temporarily takes one of those slots

Legendaries
Added - Lantern Jack's lure call now plays a distress-call sound
Added - Harpoons deflected by a legendary's shield play a varied shield-hit sound
Added - Epic fish leave a fainter purple version of the legendary trail under breach lights
Adjusted - Buried and diving legendaries and epics no longer leave a trail
Added - A foghorn sounds when a legendary haunt starts and ends

Outfitter
Added - Hovering an Outfitter fish count shows the species of that rarity aboard

Cargo and items
Fixed - Fish, crate and pile tooltips only show their right-click hints for fish in your fleet's cargo, not in markets, storage or selection screens
Adjusted - Fish art on crate labels in cargo is drawn sharper
Adjusted - Tooltips across most items
Fixed - Fish, crates and piles sold to a market now disappear when its stock refreshes

Codex
Added - Codex pages of caught fish show a size distribution chart with your best and latest catch

1.0.a
Added - Initial Mod Release

General
Adjusted - Release downloads leave out development tools, libraries and source files
Adjusted - Rewrote fishing settings descriptions to explain their effects and limits more clearly

Development
Added - Changelog and release instructions
